disableResume
==============
Do not allow the pipeline to resume if the controller restarts. For example: options { disableResume() }

In Jenkins, the disableResume option is used in conjunction with the checkout step to prevent Jenkins from attempting to resume a partially completed pipeline run from a checkpoint. 

This can be useful in situations where you want to ensure that a pipeline always starts from scratch, even if a previous run was interrupted.

pipeline {
    agent any
    stages {
        stage('Checkout') {
            steps {
               git 'https://github.com/bhanuprakash678910/mavenproj.git'
            }
        }
    }
    options {
        disableResume()
    }
}


